------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXCEPTION: src/waveguide_scattering/adaptlob.m
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

That one file is not ours to license. It is Walter Gautschi's adaptive Lobatto
quadrature routine, bylined "Walter Gautschi, 08/03/98" and implementing the
algorithm of W. Gander and W. Gautschi, "Adaptive Quadrature -- Revisited",
BIT Numerical Mathematics 40(1), 84-101 (2000), after Gander,
Computermathematik, Birkhaeuser, 1992. It reached this project as part of the
original source tree, carrying an attribution line but no license grant, and it
is redistributed here on that same basis. The only local change is a small
patch -- a `termination2` flag that limits a repeated warning to one per call,
plus a tolerance clamp -- which does not alter the quadrature.

The MIT grant above does not extend to it. Anyone redistributing this
repository who needs clean terms for that file can substitute an equivalently
licensed adaptive quadrature; note that doing so would change results at the
level of the quadrature tolerance and would require revalidating stage 2
against the shipped data.
